    "body": "# Shared scholarship research\n\nKeep one record per award in `opportunities/`; reference its ID from each relevant program dossier. This allows reuse across applications without duplicating rules or deadlines.\n\nAudience: general master's applicants, with explicit Hong Kong and Taiwan eligibility checks. Track nationality, residency, passport and any local nomination conditions separately. The user's \"Hong Kong / Taiwan\" description does not establish eligibility. Also retain broadly available international and institution-specific awards for other readers.\n\n| Award ID | Opportunity | Scope | Current status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SCH-001 | [Fulbright Foreign Student Program](opportunities/fulbright-foreign-student.md) | Potentially multiple institutions/fields, subject to country award rules | Applicant eligibility and 2027 deadline unknown |\n| SCH-002 | [Knight-Hennessy Scholars](opportunities/knight-hennessy.md) | Stanford graduate programs; exact eligibility must be checked | 2027 application closed |\n| SCH-003 | [Stanford MBA need-based fellowship](opportunities/stanford-mba-fellowship.md) | Stanford MBA only | Need assessed after admission |\n\nFor each award, track: citizenship/residency; eligible degree/field/institution; degree-date restrictions; amount and coverage; duration/renewal; separate application; nomination; deadline/timezone; required documents; service/return obligations; other-award stacking; admission dependency; and applicable program IDs. Unknown conditions remain unknown.\n\nAn award potentially applying to several programs does not mean it can be held repeatedly or simultaneously. Verify reuse, renewal and stacking separately. Keep assistantships and loans identified separately from scholarship awards.\n"
